<code>assert \old(this.inSameSet(element1, element2)) => \result == \old(this.numberOfSets()) : assert !\old(this.inSameSet(element1, element2)) => \result == \old(this.numberOfSets()) - 1;</code>

However, since the assert statement should reflect the change in the number of sets only when the elements are not initially in the same set, the correct assert statement would be:

<code>assert !\old(this.inSameSet(element1, element2)) => \result == \old(this.numberOfSets()) - 1;</code>

This ensures that the number of sets decreases by 1 only if the elements were not already in the same set.
